fact WorkItem(id: "WI-487", description: some(value: "Link op-body param variable references to the param's Symbol at load (fix op-body var <-> OperationInfo param symbol mismatch). ROOT CAUSE (diagnosed in WI-483): an op body's ?b reference to a param is a Term::Var in the parse IR; the op-body converter (load.rs visit_load) has no Term::Var arm, so ?b falls to generic convert_term which MINTS A FRESH logical var re-interning 'b' to a NEW Symbol, distinct from the param's OperationInfo Symbol (scanned SymbolKind::Param, load.rs:762). Empirically: OperationInfo param 'b'=Symbol(1485); op_body_node ?b=Expr::Var(Global) named Symbol(1572) — both 'b', different. Interpreter bridges by NAME (eval::find_local, eval.rs:1620). load_var_ref (Ident path -> remap -> param symbol) is NOT hit for ?b (a Var); build_expr_leaf/check_bare_ref preserve symbols but aren't reached. FIX: op-body variable conversion should resolve a ?b whose name matches an op param (resolve_in_scope -> SymbolKind::Param) to the param Symbol, so body var and OperationInfo share one Symbol; then find_local/WI-483 fold bind by symbol. BLAST RADIUS: op-body var identity touches typer env, eval find_local, discrim — test carefully; only param-named free vars resolve (not let/lambda/match-bound). BLOCKS WI-483. Acceptance: op_body_node param var Symbol == OperationInfo.params[i].0; full suite green."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-06-16T08:05:31Z"))
